A||N||6||justme||alternator/voltage regulator/belts?||||1||
Z||000000||justme||05-14-2001||10:58 PM||||Three things:<P>When i start the car, i have to rev the engine to get the volt light to go out and prevent it from stalling.<P>When i turn on the air conditioner, the car immediately loses all power, and if i press the accelerator the car makes popping noises and jerks during very slow and strained acceleration.<P>As i was sitting at a stoplight with the headlights on, the car started to die out and the volt light started glowing bright red. the only way to keep the car from dying was to turn out the lights.<P>any thoughts?  bad alternator or slipping belt?  something else?||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||05-14-2001||11:02 PM||||It is normal for the older style alternators to require a bit of engine rev's to get it excited and putting out.  But if the light comes back on again after it goes out you do have a problem.  Yes, it could be as simple as a loose belt.||||reg||1
Z||000002||justme||05-14-2001||11:33 PM||||after today the voltage light is permanently on, and no matter how high i rev the engine or how fast i drive, it doesn't charge or go off. the belts feel pretty tight.  the lower one looks wobbly when the car is running though.  which belt is which?||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||05-15-2001||12:10 AM||||it is the flat belt on v/6, or outer one.||||reg||1
Z||000004||justme||05-15-2001||12:41 AM||||the flat outer belt is tight, the other one looks loose.  what does the inner belt drive?||||reg||1
Z||000005||DavidHenshaw||05-15-2001||09:58 AM||||The inner belt is for your air conditioning compressor. <P>It sounds like you need a new alternator. Take it to Advance, Pep Boys or some place like that. They can drag a tester out to the car to test the charging as it runs. BTW how old is the battery?<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||justme||05-15-2001||11:03 AM||||the battery is about a year and a half. i replaced it when the engine blew. what's a fair price to pay for an alternator?||||reg||1
